{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Eevee Light Probes.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Eevee Light Probes.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"eevee light probes eevee light probes","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Eevee Light Probes.md","fileName":"Eevee Light Probes.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Eevee Light Probes","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-07 23:25\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Lighting and Rendering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Lighting and Rendering","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Eevee Light Probes.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Eevee Light Probes.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"eevee light probes eevee light probes","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Eevee Light Probes.md","fileName":"Eevee Light Probes.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Eevee Light Probes","heading":"Eevee Light Probes","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Light probes give Eevee sampled information that ordinary screen-space effects cannot obtain from objects outside the camera view. Reflection cube maps and planes support reflections, while irradiance volumes support indirect illumination.\n\nCube maps and irradiance volumes must be baked into a light cache before rendering; reflection planes update directly. Probe position, influence area, falloff, and resolution determine where the cached lighting applies and how expensive it is to compute.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Lighting and Rendering","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Eevee Light Probes.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Eevee Light Probes.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"eevee light probes eevee light probes",